; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9772   
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9773  /* Justification for module-specific MISRA deviations:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9774  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9775  MD_CanIf_Rule8.9:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9776    Reason: Constant tables are kept at a central location for a better overview and maintenance.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9777    Risk: Name conflict.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9778    Prevention: Compiler optimize and check for name conflicts.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9779  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9780  MD_CanIf_Rule9.1:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9781    Reason: The variable is set depending on the configuration, so a default value of the variable is not possible.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9782    Risk: Undefined value of the variable.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9783    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different configurations in the component test.  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9784  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9785  MD_CanIf_Rule10.5_4342:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9786    Reason: The different mode types are abstracted with the enum CanIf_PduGetModeType/ CanIf_PduSetModeType.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9787            But a lookup table CanIfState from a basic unsigned data type is used to get a requested mode.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9788            This leads to a runtime efficient code.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9789    Risk: Inconsistency between mode types in CanIf_PduGetModeType/ CanIf_PduSetModeType enum and CanIfState lookup table.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9790    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different configurations in the component test. 
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9791  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9792  MD_CanIf_Rule11.1:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9793    Reason: Cast to different pointer type required to avoid compiler warning due to usage of a union of function pointer types.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9794    Risk: None due to fact that function pointer are used.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9795    Prevention: Test of the different variants in the component test.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9796  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9797  MD_CanIf_Rule11.8:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9798    Reason: Pointer cast to P2VAR is necessary to avoid compiler warning because "SduDataPtr" within "PduInfoType" is defined
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9799            as P2VAR while "CanSduPtr" is P2CONST.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9800    Risk: CAN data could be modified after cast to P2VAR.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9801    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different variants in the component test.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9802  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9803  MD_CanIf_ErrorId:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9804    Reason: Usage of defined API pattern.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9805    Risk: Statements in this 'if' block are not executed.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9806    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different configurations in the component test.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9807  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9808  MD_CanIf_Rule14.3_GenData:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9809    Reason: Configuration related constant data.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9810    Risk: Statements in the 'if' or 'else' block are not executed.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9811    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different configurations in the component test.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9812  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9813  MD_CanIf_RxPduConstData:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9814    Reason: Configuration related Rx-PDU constant data. 
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9815    Risk: Statements in the 'if' or 'else' block are not executed.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9816    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different configurations in the component test.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9817  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9818  MD_CanIf_CanTrcvMapConstData:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9819    Reason: Configuration related CanTrcv mapping constant data.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9820    Risk: Statements in the 'if' block are not executed.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9821    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different configurations in the component test.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9822  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9823  MD_CanIf_Rule15.4:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9824    Reason: More than one break statement is used to terminate the loop during the search algorithm.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9825            This leads to more efficient code which is easier to read and maintain.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9826    Risk: Relevant fragments of code not executed.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9827    Prevention: Code inspection.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9828  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9829  MD_CanIf_Rule17.8:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9830    Reason: The direct modification of the function parameter leads to more efficient code which is easier to read and maintain.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9831    Risk: Incorrect expectation of the value of the modified function parameter.    
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9832    Prevention: Code inspection and test of the different configurations in the component test.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9833  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9834  MD_CanIf_Dir4.1_2842:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9835    Reason: Possible out of bounds read access.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9836    Risk: Wrong data access.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9837    Prevention: Test of the different configurations in the component test.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9838  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9839  */
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanIf\CanIf.c	  9840  
